{{!--
      Typefaces: Inter + Noto Sans Mono, both from Google Fonts. Requested as
      variable fonts (wght@100..900) rather than a fixed weight list, since
      --dt-typo-font-family-* is used at several different weights depending
      on scale/resolution tier (dt-tokens.css) and a variable font serves any
      of them from one file rather than a separate download per weight.
      bridge.css carries a fallback stack so an offline preview or an
      air-gapped CI still renders something.
    --}}
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@100..900&family=Noto+Sans+Mono:wght@100..900&display=swap">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{{uiRootPath}}}/css/site.css">
{{#with site.keys.homeBackground}}
    {{!--
      The landing's decorative background (GH-18, home.css). A per-site image
      that the bundle cannot ship, and a URL, so it arrives as a custom
      property rather than a stylesheet rule — declared here, in one place, so
      no element carries an inline `style` attribute. Set it in the playbook as
      `site.keys.home_background`; without it home.css falls back to `none` and
      the landing renders on a plain surface.

      Written from the site root (`site.path` + the key) rather than through
      `relativize`, which every other asset URL in this bundle uses. A relative
      URL would be wrong here: a `url()` inside a custom property is resolved
      against the stylesheet that *substitutes* it, which is site.css under the
      UI output directory, not this document. Root-absolute is the one form
      that means the same thing from both, and `site.path` carries the subpath
      when the site is published under one.
    --}}
    <style>:root { --home-background-image: url("{{@root.site.path}}{{this}}") }</style>
{{/with}}
